      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A roof inspection in Utah typically costs $0 if you use a local roofing contractor, but it ranges from $150 to $400 for a certified independent report. The final price depends primarily on is performing the inspection and why you need it.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "$150 to $400 for a certified independent report"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udcb0 Cost Breakdowns"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Free Inspections (Contractor Estimates)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you suspect you have storm damage, aging shingles, or a leak, most local Utah roofing companies will inspect your roof for free. They offer this complimentary service hoping to earn your business for any necessary repairs or replacements. Local providers like Roofing Utah , The Roofing Experience , and Rooval Roofing provide free, no-obligation assessments.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Paid Inspections (Official Reports)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you require an independent, third-party assessment for a real estate transaction, a home sale, or an insurance dispute, you will need a paid inspection.",
        "reference_indexes": [
